/* ============================================================================
   Calculating Remuneration for Servicing Advisors
   Fixes applied:
     1. Removed +7 and +1 date offsets in %ALL_OFFICE_MONTHLY_EARN macro
        — these were shifting the window and causing QA to read the wrong period
     2. Removed unused 3rd macro parameter (QA_Periods) from %ALL_OFFICE_MONTHLY_EARN
     3. Temp tables used to avoid recursive reference warnings
     4. Data type mismatch in Leave join confirmed both character — direct join used
     5. %Final_Earn macro: QA_Period forced to numeric date on both sides via
        input(put(...,date9.),date9.) to prevent format mismatch causing empty
        start_date, end_date and QA_Evaluations columns in COMP/LOC Final Earns
     6. %Final_Earn macro: strip() added to Employee_Number join to remove
        trailing spaces that can silently break the match
   ============================================================================ */

%include "/data/fnbins/fnbinsurance/Growth_Analytics/SASCODE/DEPLOYED/Automation/STI_CA_2/Libnames.sas";


/* ============================================================================
   PART 1: TIME PERIOD SETUP
   ============================================================================ */

